      "0": "Screenshots show the Slack channel view for #daytona-support with at least three substantive request messages visible in the main timeline (Ding 10:37 AM with “4 replies”; tech 2:29 AM with “1 reply”; George n “Yesterday at 12:23:09 PM” with “1 reply”). A thread pane is shown opened only for Ding’s message (“Thread in daytona-support (channel, 4 replies)”). No screenshot evidence shows opening/inspecting the threads for tech or George n, nor scrolling/loading enough history to reach up to 8 requests.",
      "1": "Requester names and timestamps are visible in-channel for multiple messages (e.g., “Ding 10:37 AM,” “tech 2:29 AM,” and George n with “Yesterday at 12:23:09 PM”). For Ding, the thread view also shows a more precise timestamp link (“Aug 27th at 10:37:05 AM. Open in channel”) in one screenshot, and another screenshot shows “Ding Thursday at 10:37 AM” in the thread header. Thus, timestamps may appear both as relative/weekday labels and as an exact date+seconds link depending on the UI area.",
      "2": "Ding’s full problem text is visible (401 error contacting Support through dashboard; sandbox ID; files owned by nobody:nogroup; root can’t read/change ownership; chown “Operation not permitted,” including a quoted related prior issue). The other two visible requests (tech unrecoverable error; George n Stripe connectivity) are only visible as brief snippets in the channel list area; their full details are not shown unless their threads/messages are opened.",
      "3": "The latest visible reply for Ding depends on which screenshot/state is referenced: one DOM view shows only Nikola’s replies up to “Permanent fix is merged and will be deployed today, please stand by” at 11:04; a later DOM view shows additional replies including “Ding Yesterday at 10:36 AM … hasn’t recovered yet” and “Dalin Stone APP Yesterday at 12:17 PM … Please check now,” making “Please check now” the latest visible reply in that later view. No screenshots show the latest responses for tech or George n threads because their threads are not opened.",
      "4": "In the Ding thread, screenshots show forward-looking/diagnostic responses (“Checking,” “Permanent fix is merged and will be deployed today, please stand by”) and later “Please check now,” plus the requester stating it “hasn’t recovered yet.” There is no explicit confirmation in the visible content that the issue is resolved (e.g., no “fixed now/thanks it works”), so any status must be based on the absence/presence of such explicit statements. Other requests’ statuses cannot be evidenced from screenshots because their thread contents are not shown.",
      "5": "Only Ding’s request has enough visible thread context to justify follow-up considerations (requester says “hasn’t recovered yet,” then support says “Please check now,” with no visible confirmation afterward). Additional recent requests (tech unrecoverable error; George n Stripe) are visible as items with threads, but screenshots do not show their thread replies, so whether they need follow-up cannot be determined from the provided visible evidence without opening those threads.",
      "6": "Across screenshots, message compose areas are visible (channel message box and thread reply box) with “Send now” buttons, but there is no evidence of text being entered or any send/edit/delete/reaction action occurring. The recorded actions shown are clicks for navigation/opening a thread (“4 replies”), which are non-modifying interactions."
